{:actor/id "deploy_verifier"
 :actor/kind :agent
 ;; The email is load-bearing, and it is the bootstrap system admin's on
 ;; purpose. The :trusted-loopback grant in
 ;; contracts/knoxx/authentication/mcp_http.edn resolves its context by
 ;; :grant/user-email, and law/token-actor-honourable? then refuses every call
 ;; unless that membership's stored actor binding equals the grant's
 ;; :grant/actor-id. Projecting this actor onto any other email would leave
 ;; the admin membership unbound and turn initialize into a 403.
 :actor/email "system-admin@open-hax.local"
 :actor/username "system-admin@open-hax.local"
 :actor/org "open-hax"
 :actor/label "Deploy Verifier"
 ;; Role projection replaces the bound membership's roles with exactly this
 ;; list (:replace true in project-actor-role-slugs!), so :role/system-admin
 ;; is not decorative: without it the bootstrap admin membership would be
 ;; demoted to the three probe tools, and the MCP catalog the gate counts
 ;; would collapse to them. :role/deploy-verifier records which tools the
 ;; gate actually exercises.
 :actor/roles [:role/system-admin :role/deploy-verifier]
 :actor/policy
 {:principal :actor
  :source-of-truth :contract
  :notes
  "The identity the post-deploy MCP gate runs as. The :trusted-loopback grant
   in contracts/knoxx/authentication/mcp_http.edn names this :grant/actor-id, so
   credential-backed tools resolve their credentials against the membership
   this contract materializes rather than borrowing whichever actor the
   system-admin membership happens to hold.

   Credentials are NOT declared here, as with open_hax: they are actor-owned
   state in the policy DB, written through
   PUT /api/admin/actors/:userId/credentials/:provider. Until a discord_bot
   credential lands on this actor, discord_list_servers reports a tool-error
   and the gate fails — which is the intended signal, not a false positive."}}
